WEBVTT

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.670
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.670
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:19.670
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.420
Chapter 5

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:44.420
One Hundred Billion Stars, One Hundred Billion Lights

00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:12.300
Idiot !

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:12.810
Don't leave here !

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:13.670
You'll get yourself killed !

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:40.200
Advance the wire
guided missile tanks !

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.160
Fire !

00:04:13.230 --> 00:04:14.320
Continue firing !

00:04:29.790 --> 00:04:30.740
Advance !

00:04:39.630 --> 00:04:40.460
Crap.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:42.540
Their missiles
are too accurate.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:43.480
How disgusting.

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.420
They're the type that
overcome microwaves.

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:49.920
Neither radio interference
nor carbon smoke seem to work.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:52.600
I suppose attacking the
shooters is the only solution.

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:58.500
Can you sever the guidance wires
with the laser, Der Decken ?

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:01.670
I'll give it a shot.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:28.670
We did it !

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:35.010
The Imperial troops had already
assaulted the base three times...

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:38.320
...but they were
repelled at every turn.

00:05:38.320 --> 00:05:41.130
Since the terrain made it difficult
for their troops to spread out...

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:45.320
...the Imperial Army couldn't use
their size advantage effectively.

00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:47.020
From the Imperial
Army's standpoint...

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:49.530
...it seemed the only method was to
continue moving in a narrow line...

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:52.030
...and wait for attrition in
the enemy defensive line.

00:05:53.370 --> 00:05:57.320
That greenhorn Schenkopp is
sustaining their defenses fairly well.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:06:00.120
But they won't
last much longer.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:05.770
That Luneberg did not move
his troops in more forcefully...

00:06:05.770 --> 00:06:10.340
...signified that he did not
underestimate Schenkopp's presence.

00:06:12.700 --> 00:06:17.320
Rather, he was
actually overestimating him

00:06:19.170 --> 00:06:25.370
Schenkopp wasn't the commander of
the Van-Fleet 4-2 base defensive line;

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:28.020
...he was merely a part of it.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:34.770
Other front-line commanders were
also sustaining good defensive efforts.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:45.320
Each regiment was putting up a good fight
despite the fact that Vice Admiral Cerebrese...

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:49.120
...had spread out their defensive
line so far horizontally...

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:51.740
...that it made communications between
the regiments nearly impossible.

00:06:54.700 --> 00:07:01.070
For one thing, because this was a rear-line
support base, they had abundant ammunition.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:10.360
If there was a weakness in the Alliance defensive line it was the base commander Vice Admiral Cerebrese.

00:07:15.250 --> 00:07:18.360
At this rate, the enemy will
seize total control of the sky.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:19.560
What are you planning to do,
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp ?

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.770
Should I send them
a radio communication...

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:26.370
...and tell them to repent and
return control of the sky to us ?

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:34.320
That Schenkopp is
getting arrogant.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.700
This is why I don't
trust the Rosenritter.

00:07:37.540 --> 00:07:40.560
Then why don't you just tell him that,
without ending the radio communication ?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:43.770
Report the present
battle situation !

00:07:43.770 --> 00:07:46.370
The conditions are getting even worse !
No sign of changing for the better !

00:07:58.650 --> 00:08:00.410
What do you think,
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp ?

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:01.390
What are your predictions ?

00:08:01.760 --> 00:08:02.910
I haven't the slightest idea.

00:08:02.910 --> 00:08:08.440
I can predict the outcomes of battles,
but this is an ill-natured gamble.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:14.150
Lt. Colonel, how can
you put up with him ?

00:08:14.150 --> 00:08:16.210
It's just a service.

00:08:17.150 --> 00:08:21.730
I sympathize with the
Vice Admiral a little bit.

00:08:21.730 --> 00:08:22.910
You sympathize ?

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:28.110
I thought you hated
the Vice Admiral, but...

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:29.540
Of course I hate him.

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:34.570
But an expert at desk work was thrown
into actual combat all of a sudden.

00:08:34.570 --> 00:08:37.470
We all have strengths
and weaknesses.

00:08:37.470 --> 00:08:43.100
Not everyone can be as fearless and
daring as Walter von Schenkopp.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:44.880
I'm in awe.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.120
But...

00:08:47.770 --> 00:08:54.220
...it's frustrating to have to fight
under an amateur in a battle like this.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:13.780
This is the image from the
reconnaissance planes we sent earlier.

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.370
As I thought, our rear-line
base is being attacked.

00:09:17.020 --> 00:09:18.360
Where is the Imperial Fleet ?

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.820
They're deployed on
the north pole.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:22.530
There's no sign of
them in satellite orbit.

00:09:23.980 --> 00:09:25.020
Isn't that strange ?

00:09:25.020 --> 00:09:26.570
What are they trying to do ?

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:32.290
They might have thought that if they stayed in
orbit, they might draw attention to themselves.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:36.760
Regardless of their intentions,
there's no time to waste.

00:09:36.760 --> 00:09:39.850
We'll shut down the
head of their fleet.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:40.760
Hurry.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.500
Understood.

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:46.100
At this point, we
have the advantage.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.310
But I don't think the main
Imperial Fleet will stay put.

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:51.780
We should ask for
reinforcements, shouldn't we ?

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:52.800
Yes, we'll do
so immediately.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:09:58.980
It's an emergency.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:02.230
The enemy fleet is
closing in on this area !

00:10:03.770 --> 00:10:04.630
Why ?

00:10:04.630 --> 00:10:06.140
Why is the
enemy coming here ?

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:15.320
Please give all
ships orders to launch.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:18.630
At this stage, we can't be
bothered with the enemy base !

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:22.300
If they attack us from orbit,
our fleet will be decimated !

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:30.850
But we must first send orders
to the ground troops to retreat.

00:10:30.850 --> 00:10:33.220
There's no time for that.

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:39.370
But we can't abandon
our ground troops.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:45.270
Especially since Commodore Musel is
the brother of Countess Grunewald.

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:50.960
If we leave him behind, it'll be a more
serious issue than just a bad reputation.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.240
T...that's...

00:10:56.580 --> 00:11:00.510
In any case, we will send retreat
orders to the ground troops...

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:03.670
...and also call for reinforcements
from Fleet Headquarters.

00:11:05.870 --> 00:11:11.840
Even before the report from Grimmelshausen, Imperial Fleet Headquarters...

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:14.840
...had already detected the
movement of the Alliance 5th Fleet.

00:11:16.500 --> 00:11:22.900
As I thought, that enemy fleet was
moving toward Van-Fleet 4-2.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:28.590
But the Grimmelshausen Fleet was
outside our plans to begin with.

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:31.320
I suspect it might be more
advisable to abandon them...

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:34.350
...rather than going to their rescue and
risking casualties to our main fleet.

00:11:34.350 --> 00:11:41.020
You may be right, but since the enemy movements have become clear we can't just sit here and watch.

00:11:41.020 --> 00:11:45.220
Send orders to all ships to move
in on Van-Fleet 4-2 immediately.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:46.200
Hurry.

00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:46.700
Yes, sir.

00:11:47.790 --> 00:11:50.500
A large enemy fleet has
been detected to our rear.

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:54.600
As I thought,
they're gathering here.

00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.130
This doesn't look
good, does it ?

00:11:56.130 --> 00:12:04.780
No, if their main fleet had moved in sooner,
we would have been attacked in this area.

00:12:04.780 --> 00:12:07.630
I'd like to think the present
situation is better than that.

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:13.220
But since the opposition has made a
definitive move, wouldn't it be advisable...

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:17.500
...for you to request a change
of plans from Headquarters ?

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:22.000
Commander...

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:31.400
The staff at Headquarters doesn't like it when
I give my opinions on the larger battle plan.

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:35.010
Perhaps you're worrying too much ?

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:40.850
No, because I'm not from a military school,
I'm not well-liked among the school cliques.

00:12:40.850 --> 00:12:44.680
I'm used to fighting
a solitary war.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:45.830
Commander...

00:12:47.130 --> 00:12:50.330
But I think we'll
be okay this time.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:54.550
I've reported the situation
to Borodin of the 12th Fleet.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:13:00.630
He will make his own decision and come to our
rescue, without orders from Headquarters.

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:30.370
The situation was chaotic
on the ground also.

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:33.630
Reinhard was also
fighting under gunfire.

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:38.020
As he was a sub-captain to Luneberg
and did not have command of the troops...

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:41.160
...he, unlike his usual self,
remained indecisive in his actions.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.820
Kircheis, what's the overall 
battle situation like right now ?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:52.630
That's impossible to
answer, Lord Reinhard.

00:13:52.630 --> 00:13:53.950
You're right.

00:13:53.950 --> 00:13:57.390
If there's anyone who does
know, they're not human.

00:14:07.500 --> 00:14:13.800
Lord Reinhard, if I may say so, I'd like you to
focus on the combat in front of us for now.

00:14:13.800 --> 00:14:19.770
And once you accomplish your personal
objectives, it'd be better to return to the fleet.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.840
Please don't concern yourself
with the larger picture.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:25.710
Kircheis, I never thought
you'd recommend selfishness.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:27.300
But we'll do as you say.

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.370
This is a meaningless battle anyway.

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:32.700
At least, we'll come out of this
with personal accomplishments.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.450
Charge !

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:23.790
All of you, take
the right route !

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:24.580
Vice Admiral Bucock, the situation hasn't
changed for the better, so what do we do ?

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:28.370
There's no need to
be so pessimistic.

00:16:28.370 --> 00:16:35.700
In the battles I've experienced, there weren't
many in which we were in good shape.

00:16:37.130 --> 00:16:38.020
I see.

00:16:38.620 --> 00:16:39.700
It's our allies !

00:16:39.700 --> 00:16:41.810
The 12th Fleet has arrived !

00:16:43.060 --> 00:16:44.010
Oh, well.

00:16:44.010 --> 00:16:46.480
Borodin has finally arrived.

00:16:46.480 --> 00:16:49.200
But I'm sure it
was a bother for him.

00:16:55.990 --> 00:17:00.760
The Van-Fleet 4-2 Area is
too small for a fleet battle.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:09.220
Regardless, Borodin attempted to
maintain some distance first...

00:17:09.220 --> 00:17:12.250
...and forge the right formation for a
battle to maintain his tactical advantage.

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:19.360
But just before the fleet completed its
formation, other Alliance fleets arrived...

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:23.320
...and they pushed the 12th Fleet
forward into the combat area.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:29.370
So Borodin's strategy did not come to fruition,
and all the fleets blindly went into the battle.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.630
Don't fire without thinking !

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:36.560
You might shoot
down our allies !

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:39.160
Can't you do something
about the traffic ?!

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:40.910
Where should we go ?!

00:17:56.050 --> 00:17:57.390
What's going on
with the engine ?

00:17:57.390 --> 00:17:58.780
It can't be repaired !

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.040
At this rate, we'll
fall on the satellite !

00:18:01.820 --> 00:18:03.440
There's no other way:
we'll abandon ship.

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.320
All hands, abandon ship !

00:18:05.770 --> 00:18:07.120
All hands, abandon ship !

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:08.560
All hands, abandon ship !

00:18:35.450 --> 00:18:38.180
This is so chaotic.

00:18:38.180 --> 00:18:44.670
If the Imperial Fleet has a
solution for this, I'd like to hear it.

00:18:47.060 --> 00:18:52.020
What's the situation
with Van-Fleet 4-2 ?

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:59.360
Order the Grimmelshausen Fleet
to report the situation.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:04.270
And tell them to lift off and move in on the
rear guard of the enemy fleet, if they can.

00:19:04.920 --> 00:19:05.770
Yes, sir !

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:09.390
Why do I have to give him such a
common sense order like this ?

00:19:09.390 --> 00:19:14.770
He should stop ground combat
immediately and come out to space.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:16.390
What good are our ships
if they're on the ground ?

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:25.840
Colonel Luneberg...

00:19:26.900 --> 00:19:29.550
If I remember, your
name was Der Decken.

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:32.860
I recognize
that fat figure.

00:19:32.860 --> 00:19:36.100
Did you get a little more used
to combat these past three years ?

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:39.400
As your former regimental leader,
I'll give you a test.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:41.490
Colonel, you're a traitor.

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:46.070
After you left us, do you
know how we were treated ?

00:19:46.070 --> 00:19:51.910
All officers were brought to court martial,
and the regiment was about to be dissolved.

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:53.210
It's all because of you !

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.850
You and your
noisy yellow beak !

00:19:56.850 --> 00:20:00.750
Since when have the Rosenritter been taught
to use their tongues more than their arms ?

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.820
As soon as I left,
you all grew so frail.

00:20:03.820 --> 00:20:05.900
What a pitiful disgrace !

00:20:10.530 --> 00:20:11.520
Lt. Colonel Schenkopp !

00:20:12.800 --> 00:20:14.000
That idiot !

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:18.090
I told everyone not
to engage Luneberg.

00:20:18.090 --> 00:20:20.370
I'm the only one who can
put up a fight against him !

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:39.000
Lord Reinhard...

00:21:02.010 --> 00:21:03.860
He's guarded very well.

00:21:37.950 --> 00:21:39.250
He's strong.

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.700
I've never met an enemy
as skilled as he is.

00:21:42.880 --> 00:21:46.930
If Lord Reinhard had to fight
a dangerous man like this...

00:21:49.040 --> 00:21:51.420
I can't believe he's
withstanding my offense.

00:21:52.050 --> 00:21:53.460
Who is he ?

00:21:53.460 --> 00:21:57.650
I didn't know there were still intrepid men like
this in the Imperial Army, aside from Luneberg.

00:21:57.650 --> 00:22:01.480
I don't know why, but even though their
military as a whole has fallen to depravity...

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.130
...good talents still
come out of it.

00:22:05.660 --> 00:22:07.070
I'd like to know your name.

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:24.560
I must find Lord Reinhard !

00:22:46.070 --> 00:22:48.450
Hey, Der Decken !

00:23:10.120 --> 00:23:11.710
Wait, Luneberg !

00:23:16.960 --> 00:23:19.450
You should have said "please."

00:23:19.450 --> 00:23:22.200
I was your regimental leader.

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:25.570
You threw away that
position yourself.

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:27.410
So don't you dare
act like my superior !

00:23:27.410 --> 00:23:31.910
Right now, you're just a two-legged dog in
the care of the Empire's high aristocrats.

00:23:31.910 --> 00:23:36.600
For you to speak human
language - it's blasphemy.

00:23:39.590 --> 00:23:40.220
What ?

00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:47.790
Der Decken is
waiting for you.

00:23:47.790 --> 00:23:50.850
Be glad to go to Valhalla, Hell,
or whatever you call it !

00:24:08.410 --> 00:24:09.190
Lt. Colonel !

00:24:11.110 --> 00:24:11.950
Dammit !

00:24:16.890 --> 00:24:18.510
Lt. Colonel, are you alright ?

00:24:19.890 --> 00:24:20.800
Yeah.

00:24:23.670 --> 00:24:27.860
At this point, the Imperial Fleet had
already sent an order to retreat.

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:31.570
But in a disorderly condition where
even the commander, Luneberg...

00:24:31.570 --> 00:24:35.320
...was in the
thick of combat...

00:24:35.320 --> 00:24:37.300
...there was no one who
could execute that order.

00:24:38.580 --> 00:24:43.400
Because of that, the chaos was to continue on for a while.

00:24:39.910 --> 00:24:46.670
A Dangerous Man

00:24:48.600 --> 00:24:57.800
 Even as I say it's beautiful. Even as I say it's magnificent

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:52.940
[ Aurora's Adagio ]

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:52.940
Ending Theme

00:24:48.720 --> 00:24:52.940
